  "description": "Florida's 13th Congressional District, covering Pinellas County on the Gulf Coast, will hold its 2026 election for U.S. Representative. Republican incumbent Anna Paulina Luna, first elected in 2022 and re-elected in 2024, is seeking a third term in a district with an R+5 partisan lean. Democrats view the seat as a top pickup opportunity and have recruited a crowded primary field including retired Army Brigadier General Leela Gray, who has earned EMILY's List endorsement. The August 18, 2026 Democratic primary will determine who challenges Luna in the November general election. Key issues in the race include affordability, public safety, veterans' affairs, and reproductive rights.",
